From 62f337f4046e55037995af260433dcbd1d203a2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darcy Phipps <dphipps@qnx.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Mar 2025 15:21:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 59/60] Fix missing dependencies making QT plugin

When trying to build VLC for x86_64 I ran into a problem making the QT
plugin with missing dependencies. This led down a rabbit hole of trying
to track dependencies and where they come from.

The dependencies for a given plugin are discovered by configure by
looking at the associated .pc file. In this case contrib's Qt5Gui.pc
lists, among other things, fontconfig as a dependency. Thus automake
adds -lfontconfig to the link command line for the QT plugin.

fontconfig has its own dependencies, the relevant ones for this
discussion are libxml2 and liblzma.

At this point, libtool takes over. It looks at the various .la files
that were created to find any transitive dependencies. It correctly
identifies that libfontconfig.la wants libxml2 and liblzma, however
since I'm making a shared object instead of a program it doesn't add
them to the link. Thus any unresolved symbols from libfontconfig will
likely remain unresolved, breaking the build.

I don't think there is a way to get either libtool or configure to deal
with this without major surgery. Instead I noticed that the Makefile.am
that creates the QT plugin target adds the following variables to the
link: QT_LIBS (which is set by configure), LIBS_qt (which appears to not
be set by anyone and is empty) and LIBM.

LIBS_qt, being empty, seems an obvious choice. So for the QNX build set
it to hold the missing libraries (and anything THEY depend on).

This got the build going for the QT plugin and luckily nothing else
seems to have this problem. Ideally a global solution would be better
but as long as this is the only failure of this kind, this specific
solution is good enough.

An interesting side note, this only breaks the x86_64 build. The
aarch64le build, in theory, should have the same problem but it does
not. For whatever reason, libfontconfig built for Arm64 doesn't seem to
depend on the same unresolved symbols. This probably is worth further
investigation when there is time.
---
 qnx/common.mk | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/qnx/common.mk b/qnx/common.mk
index 1858b4681a1..ad7e2289f59 100644
--- a/qnx/common.mk
+++ b/qnx/common.mk
@@ -128,6 +128,8 @@ VLC_CFG_ARGS += --host=${VLC_HOST} \
 		--with-contrib=$(CURDIR)/${VLC_HOST} \
 		--prefix=$(CURDIR)/install
 
+VLC_MAKE_ENV := LIBS_qt="-lfreetype -lz -lxml2 -llzma"
+
 # Currently x86_64 does not support audio/ALSA
 ifneq "$(CPU)" "x86_64"
     VLC_CFG_ARGS += --enable-alsa

From 924155c4a4c3a9dfed0b457199fb46a9197936c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darcy Phipps <dphipps@qnx.com>
Date: Fri, 2 May 2025 14:47:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 60/60] Fix broken build

Fix a couple of build breaks

(1)
The host protoc build was failing when using a newer docker container.
This is probably because it has a newer version of libstdc++ in it.
Luckily, protobuf already had a fix for it (from 2017!) that I can apply
to make the failure go away.

(2)
libgpg-error was failing to build. It was supposed to look for
lock-obj-pub.nto-qnx8.0.0.h but instead it was looking for
lock-obj-pub.nto-qnx.h.

I'm not sure why this changed, or even if it changed. Perhaps I had a
stale file before that was allowing it to pass. In any case, the two
files are identical at the moment. Just check in a versions under both
names to get things going and (possibly) protect against older systems
wanting the old name.
---
 contrib/src/gpg-error/lock-obj-pub.nto-qnx.h  | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../0001-const-FieldDescriptorCompare.patch   | 11 ++++++++++
 contrib/src/protobuf/rules.mak                |  1 +
 3 files changed, 33 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 contrib/src/gpg-error/lock-obj-pub.nto-qnx.h
 create mode 100644 contrib/src/protobuf/0001-const-FieldDescriptorCompare.patch

diff --git a/contrib/src/gpg-error/lock-obj-pub.nto-qnx.h b/contrib/src/gpg-error/lock-obj-pub.nto-qnx.h
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..5bdaa3b6b38
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/src/gpg-error/lock-obj-pub.nto-qnx.h
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## lock-obj-pub.aarch64-unknown-nto-qnx8.0.0.h
+## File created by gen-posix-lock-obj - DO NOT EDIT
+## To be included by mkheader into gpg-error.h
+
+typedef struct
+{
+  long _vers;
+  union {
+    volatile char _priv[8];
+    long _x_align;
+    long *_xp_align;
+  } u;
+} gpgrt_lock_t;
+
+#define GPGRT_LOCK_INITIALIZER {1,{{0,0,0,128,0,0,0,0}}}
+##
+## Local Variables:
+## mode: c
+## buffer-read-only: t
+## End:
+##
diff --git a/contrib/src/protobuf/0001-const-FieldDescriptorCompare.patch b/contrib/src/protobuf/0001-const-FieldDescriptorCompare.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..1de290c9f4e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/src/protobuf/0001-const-FieldDescriptorCompare.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+--- a/src/google/protobuf/compiler/java/java_file.cc
++++ b/src/google/protobuf/compiler/java/java_file.cc
